.TH ASIDE 1 2026-10-17 aside "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aside \- a keyboard-summoned AI chat panel for Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aside
.RB [ \-\-model " model" ]
.RB [ \-\-base\-url " url" ]
.br
.B aside \-\-preview
.I file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aside
opens a chat panel on the current Wayland session, streams the answer to your
question into it as the answer is generated, keeps the conversation going while
the panel is open, and leaves nothing behind: the transcript lives in this
process's memory and dies with it.
.PP
Typed input goes through
.BR zwp_text_input_v3 ,
so an input method (fcitx, ibus) can compose text.  Answers are plain wrapped
text: there is no Markdown, code-block or table rendering.
.PP
The panel is a
.B wlr\-layer\-shell
surface on the overlay layer, anchored to the top of the output 32 pixels down
and centred: a 640-pixel panel, one row tall, with the transcript below it.
The frame and the bar are the ones
.BR wlmenu (1)
draws: a translucent body with a hairline border inside a 24-pixel drop shadow,
and a 3-pixel scroll indicator at the right edge while the transcript overflows.
The transcript is a stack of blocks: a question is a bare row, while an answer, a
failure and the panel's own notes are drawn inside a rounded card inset by the
panel padding, with 8 pixels of padding above and below the text, and blocks are
separated by an 8-pixel gap.  The highlighted line is marked by a 2-pixel rail in
the left margin.
While a request is out the panel is a 60-pixel square showing four blinking
squares.  The expanded panel never exceeds the output height less 64 pixels, and
scrolls inside that limit.
.PP
The provider request is made by one
.BR curl (1)
process inside one
.BR bwrap (1)
sandbox.  The sandbox has the network and nothing else, and the API key is
handed to
.B curl
on standard input rather than as an argument, so it appears in no process list.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-model " model"
Ask this model.  Default
.IR deepseek/deepseek\-v4.1\-flash .
.TP
.BI \-\-base\-url " url"
Provider base URL.  Default
.IR https://api.commandcode.ai/provider/v1 .
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy " url"
Send the request through this proxy: any scheme
.BR curl (1)
accepts, for example
.IR socks5h://127.0.0.1:1080 .
Without it the request goes direct; the sandbox runs with an empty environment,
so
.I http_proxy
and friends have no effect.  A proxy that terminates TLS sees the question and
the credential.
.TP
.BI \-\-preview " file"
Render a scripted conversation to
.I file
as a PPM image and exit, without opening a window or contacting a provider.
This is how the layout is checked on a machine with no compositor.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
Send the typed question.
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel a streaming answer.  With no answer streaming, close the panel.
.TP
.B Up ", " Down
Move the highlighted transcript line.
.TP
.B PageUp ", " PageDown
Move it one page.
.TP
.B Alt+C
Copy the highlighted line to the clipboard with
.BR wl\-copy (1).
.TP
.B Left ", " Right ", " Home ", " End ", " Backspace ", " Delete
Edit the input line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Left ", " Ctrl+Right
Move the caret by a word.
.PP
There is no newline key: the input is one logical line that soft-wraps, and a
multi-line question can be pasted.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COMMAND_CODE_API_KEY
The provider credential.  Required: without it
.B aside
writes one line to standard error and exits non-zero without opening a window.
.TP
.B ASIDE_MODEL ", " ASIDE_BASE_URL ", " ASIDE_PROXY
Overridden by the matching flag, overriding the configuration file.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the configuration file is looked for.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Where the single-instance socket lives, so that a second launch raises the
running panel instead of opening a second window.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/aside/config.toml
Read, never written.  Flat
.I key = "value"
lines, with
.IR model ,
.I base_url
and
.I proxy
recognised.  No credential may be stored here.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The panel closed normally, including when the compositor ended the session while it
was open.
.TP
.B 1
The session could not be used: no compositor, no usable font, the panel was
refused before it appeared (the compositor closed the connection, reported an
error of its own, or never configured the window), or the sandbox could not
start.
.TP
.B 2
The configuration was refused: a missing or unreadable credential, or a
malformed configuration file.
.SH SECURITY
The provider request runs inside
.BR bwrap (1)
with
.BR \-\-unshare\-all \-\-share\-net
and an empty environment.  Inside it there is no home directory, no
.BR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR ,
no Wayland socket, no configuration file and no writable path; only the system
library tree, the name-resolution files, the certificate store, and the network
are bound.  When the sandbox cannot start, no request is sent and no unsandboxed
.B curl
is run.
.PP
What this does not cover: the network is reachable without restriction, so the
provider sees the question and anything able to intercept the connection sees
it too; the credential is readable by any process running as the same user; and
the panel itself is not sandboxed.
.SH PRIVACY
The question, the request body, the response bytes and the rendered answer live
in memory.  Nothing is written to disk: the only path opened for writing during
a normal run is none, and the only file a run ever reads is the configuration.
No history, cache or state directory is created or read.
.PP
Diagnostics go to standard error only and never contain the question, the
answer, or the key.  Whether the parent redirects standard error into a journal
is outside the program's control.
.PP
Copying a line with
.B Alt+C
is the one deliberate way text leaves: after that,
.B wl\-copy
serves the line to any application that asks for the clipboard, and its process
outlives the panel.  The compositor, and anything able to read the screen or the
process's memory as the same user, are outside the guarantee.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bwrap (1),
.BR curl (1),
.BR wl\-copy (1)
